{title: 514 - Lord of Our Life}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #514 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 514}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Lord of our [Bbm]life, and God of [Db/Ab]our [Ab7]salvation,
[Cdim]Star of our [Bbm]night, [C7]and hope of every [Db]nation,
[Gb]Hear [Fm]and receive Thy [Bbm]church's supplication,
[Db]Lord God Almighty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Lord, Thou canst [Bbm]help when earthly [Db/Ab]armor [Ab7]faileth;
[Cdim]Lord, Thou canst [Bbm]save [C7]when deadly [Fm]sin assaileth;
[Gb]Lord, [Fm]o'er Thy rock nor [Bbm]death nor [Gb]hell prevaileth;
[Db]Grant us Thy peace, Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Peace in our [Bbm]hearts our evil [Db/Ab]thoughts [Ab7]assuaging;
[Cdim]Peace in Thy [Bbm]church, [C7]where brothers [Fm]are engaging;
[Gb]Peace, [Fm]when the world its [Bbm]busy [Gb]war is waging;
[Db]Send us, O Savior.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]Grant us Thy [Bbm]help till foes are [Db/Ab]backward [Ab7]driven;
[Cdim]Grant them Thy [Bbm]truth [C7]that they may [Fm]be forgiven;
[Gb]Grant [Fm]peace on earth, and, [Bbm]after [Gb]we have striven,
[Db]Peace in Thy heaven.
{end_of_verse}
